# Store every text file with LF and check it out the same way.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is a common Windows default. Without this pin it would
# check the repo out as CRLF, and `prettier --check` — which this project
# configures with `endOfLine: "lf"` — would then fail on *every* file right
# after a fresh clone. Pinning the eol here makes the checkout independent of
# the machine's git config instead of depending on each contributor guessing
# the right `core.autocrlf` value.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
